\section{Conclusion}
In conclusion, this work addresses the computational challenges of LLM inference on edge devices through  \textit{voting-based} KV cache eviction, \textit{flexible-product} dataflow, \textit{element-serial scheduling}, a pioneering algorithm-hardware-dataflow tri-optimizations. 
% The proposed \textit{voting-based} KV cache eviction method enhances both efficiency and accuracy, while the \textit{flexible-product} dataflow with a runtime reconfigurable PE array handles dynamic sequence lengths and irregular memory accesses. Additionally, the \textit{element-serial scheduling} effectively reduces latency for nonlinear operations. 
The resulting accelerator, \textit{VEDA}, demonstrates significant performance improvements, enabling efficient LLM inference on resource-constrained platforms, and promoting real-time processing and data privacy.
