\label{app:phi_unique}

Let $D$ be a \ac{SePa} graph. In this section, we show the following lemma.

\begin{lemma}
    The parameter $\phi(D)$ is well-defined, \ie it does not depend on the choice of the binary decomposition tree of $D$.
\end{lemma}

To show that the parameter $\phi(D)$ is unique, we consider what we call the \emph{contracted decomposition tree} of $D$.
Given a binary decomposition tree $T_b$ of $D$, the contracted decomposition tree $T_c$ is obtained by merging adjacent vertices labeled with the same composition (series or parallel).
For example, the contracted decomposition tree for \Cref{fig:sepa-decomposition-tree} is shown in~\Cref{fig:contracted-sepa-decomposition-tree}.
The concept of contracted decomposition trees is not new, \eg in \cite{Bodlaender} it was called a ``minimal sp-tree''. Also the fact that the contracted decomposition tree is unique also seems to be a well-known statement (this is stated but not proven in \cite{Bodlaender}). For the sake of completeness, we give a proof of \Cref{lem:ContrComposTree} here.

