\cref{fig:nsd_scatterplot} provides scatter plot showing the performance of visual decoding models on the NSD dataset in terms of structural alignment (BASIC-L) and semantic alignment (BASIC-H). Each point represents a model, revealing trade-offs between spatial fidelity and semantic coherence. Models closer to the top-right demonstrate stronger performance across both dimensions.
For structural alignment, NeuroPictor~\cite{huo2024neuropictor}, STTM~\cite{liu2025see}, and MindEye2~\cite{scotti2024mindeye2} achieve the highest BASIC-L scores, reflecting better spatial reconstruction. In contrast, semantic alignment (BASIC-H) is best captured by NeuroVLA~\cite{shen2024neuro}, DREAM~\cite{xia2024dream}, and STTM~\cite{liu2025see}, indicating superior semantic preservation.
