	Figure \ref{dcc256} illustrates the relationship between the number of correlated columns and the threshold value $\psi_{\rm th}$ for the three deployment cases described in section III-B. For instance, in deployment case 1, where the RIS is near the BS, the maximum number of correlated elements occurs at $\psi_{\rm th} = 31^{\circ}$ for $\Delta G^{\rm dB} = 3$ and at $\psi_{\rm th} = 30^{\circ}$ for $\Delta G^{\rm dB} = 6$, indicating optimal threshold values for these configurations. At lower threshold values, such as $\psi_{\rm th} = 15^{\circ}$, all scenarios exhibit a notably reduced number of correlated columns. This suggests that increasing $\psi_{\rm th}$ enhances the correlation among the columns. Furthermore, the variation in the correlation trends across the three cases underscores the significant impact of the deployment configuration on the nature of the correlation.

