\section{Dataset}

\subsection{Dataset Overview}

As shown in Table \ref{tab:dataset_overview}, \dataset{} is composed of real-world code from established HLS benchmarks~\cite{Polybench, reagen2014machsuite, hara2008chstone, zhou2018rosetta, Vitis_Examples}, along with synthetic code generated from a variety of algorithms~\cite{li2025deepcircuitx, LeetCode}. The kernels represent the C++ source code without pragma, while the designs capture the kernel variations created by embedding different types and factors of HLS pragmas.  On average, each kernel in \dataset{} have 800.9 designs, 9.4 pragmas, and 394.4 tokens in average, indicating the complex code structures and diverse pragma design space within the dataset. An overview of the dataset construction workflow is presented in Figure \ref{fig:overview}.







