\begin{lemma}\label{lem:hnrandom}
$h \ \| \ h(n)$ is $O(\secp^{-2\gamma})$-close to uniformly random.    
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
It follows from the Leftover Hash Lemma (\cite{Vadhan12}, Theorem 6.18), which guarantees that $h \| h(n)$ is $\eps^2$ close to uniform.
For our setting of parameters it gives us that $h \| h(n) $ is $O(\secp^{-2\gamma})$-close to uniform.   
\end{proof}

