    To do that it is enough to set the precision parameter $P = \poly(\secp)$ as guaranteed by Theorem~\ref{thm:recoveringworks}.
    Conditioned on the fact that $\mathsf{RecoverRand}$ recovers enough bits, $M'$ will recover $m$ with high probability and return $M(m)$.

    \item{Condition 2.} We bound the probability that when $M'$ (defined via Algorithm~\ref{alg:maliciousllmformal}) receives a prompt generated by $G$ it returns in Line~\ref{line:returnharmful}, i.e., it returns a harmful output.
