    and so, by the union bound, the probability that at least one of $m$'s belongs to $S_H$ is at most $O(\secp^{2\gamma} \cdot |S_H|/2^{l_m})$.
    From the assumption that $\log(|S_H|) \leq l_m - \Omega(\log(\secp))$ it follows that $\gamma$ can be set so that the probability that $M'$ returns in Line~\ref{line:returnharmful} is at most $\secp^{-\Omega(1)}$.
    By construction, if $M'$ returns in the Line~\ref{line:returnnormal}, it returns $M(z)$, thus returning from the same distribution.

    \item{Condition 3.} Implied by Lemmas~\ref{lem:hnrandom},~\ref{lem:hardcore}, and~\ref{lem:equaldistribution} and the fact that the probability that $r \in \Z_n^*$ (note that it is sampled from $\Z_n$) is negligible in $\secp$.
\end{itemize}

\end{proof}

