\subsubsection{Hardware-based preemptive scheduling}
\label{P3}
This scheduling relies on specific hardware mechanisms to support preemption. This reduces the overhead of task switching and enables faster responses to real-time events. Systems like those proposed by Lin et al. \cite{Lin2016} use hardware features for lightweight context switching, ensuring that high-priority tasks meet strict deadlines while maintaining system performance. Hardware-based solutions are especially useful in latency-sensitive environments where responsiveness is critical. Table \ref{hw} provides an overview of preemptive scheduling methods (hardware-based). A detailed discussion of these methods is provided in the book.

