\subsubsection{Analysis for Power Consumption:}
Figure~\ref{fig:Power} further confirms that EcoVector consumes noticeably less energy than its baselines. The primary reason is EcoVector’s strategy of subdividing the dataset into small cluster-based graphs (as shown in Figure~\ref{fig:Distribution}a), thus reducing CPU-based distance computations—the dominant factor in mobile power usage. While additional disk reads occur, the decrease in CPU-intensive tasks provides a net power advantage.


\begin{figure}[h]
