\subsection{Sequence Analysis}
This involves examining text to extract valuable information. %, crucial for text classification and sentiment analysis.
% 
A sequence is an ordered list of elements or events following a specific pattern, whether temporal or sequential. Analyzing the identified NER entities and action verbs within their context helps reconstruct the sequence and logic of attack steps. 
% The process of analyzing series of terms or characters in a text to extract useful information from it is called sequence analysis. This examination is fundamental for various NLP tasks such as text classification and sentiment analysis. A sequence refers to an ordered list of elements or events that happen in a given pattern; this pattern can either be temporal or sequential. The identified NER entities and actions verbs should be analyzed together with their context so as to reconstruct the sequence and logic of attack steps.
Advanced techniques focus on entity aggregation, sequence reconstruction, step identification, and step aggregation, each playing a distinct role in interpreting structured data.
% Sequence analysis utilizes different advanced techniques for examining and interpreting structured data sequences. These methods concentrate on entity aggregation, sequence reconstruction, step identification, step aggregation, hierarchical structuring etc., where each technique plays a unique role in structured data analysis.

